[REQUIREMENT]
UID: MODEL-005
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Charge history, derivative and observer boundaries
STATEMENT: >>>
Constant-charge diode BE residuals/Jacobians shall retain both terminal signs and C/h derivatives without changing accepted history. Current and previous charge states shall remain representable independently of time-step scaling. Model-domain violations in an explicit initial state shall fail before observer publication. Existing thermal-voltage conduction limiting remains explicit; no broader limiting guarantee is inferred.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: src/newton.rs and src/configured.rs. Verification: tests/model_charge.rs independent two-terminal BE equations, central-difference Jacobian, overflowing previous charge hidden by large h and invalid initial observer rejection. Broader convergence/limiting sweeps follow separately.
<<<
