  VALUE: MODEL-002

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Derived campaign scope, Draft. Compose the existing bounded Shockley current law with an explicit constant parallel capacitance. Q=C*V, dQ/dV=C and E=C*V^2/2 use P-to-N voltage, positive-terminal coulombs, farads and joules. Reuse existing capacitor validation and signed Q stamps; no new numerical dependency is justified for this linear charge law. Existing diode constructors/wire representation shall remain intact through an explicit new profile.

Primary reference reviewed 2026-10-26: https://ngspice.sourceforge.io/docs/ngspice-manual.pdf, development manual 47+, September 28 2026, sections 7.2.1/7.2.2. Its diode charge depends on CJO/VJ/M and transport time TT; M defaults to 0.5. The proposed narrow CJO mapping requires explicit M=0 and no unsupported nonzero transport/series terms. This is not the default voltage-dependent junction model. Installed external-oracle provenance remains separate from the manual version.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: MODEL-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Constant parallel charge equation and finite SI contributions
STATEMENT: >>>
The bounded constant-capacitance profile shall require finite positive C and finite terminal V, return signed Q=C*V, derivative C and nonnegative E=C*V^2/2, and reject nonfinite contributions without clipping. Energy evaluation shall avoid avoidable V-squared intermediate overflow. It shall not infer unknown physical parameters or claim voltage-dependent depletion/transport charge.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: src/charge.rs reuses model::CapacitorModel. Verification: tests/model_charge.rs analytic signs/units/derivative/even energy, invalid domains, representable scaled energy and overflow rejection. Generated/model-composition evidence follows.
<<<
